  "limitations": [
    "Verus proves the actual receipt controller and HashSet mutations conditional on ENV-STRING-KEY; String key law, dispatcher, decoding, frame/replay durability and index reconstruction correspondence remain unproved.",
    "GCReceipt is a one-pack finite model; the unbounded single-pack deletion proof is not extended through receipt persistence/recovery or composed with the full multi-pack adapter.",
    "Receipts require successful truthful directory barriers, stable no-reuse paths and compliant peers. Valid forged receipts and external path recreation are outside the environment contract.",
    "Each nonempty completed batch adds a catalog receipt append/sync; permanent tombstones/log growth, cold replay and collection-capacity costs remain.",
    "Measurements are warm repeated calls in one-directory pools with ascending levels and balanced binary order; cache/backend load is uncontrolled. First-call costs have only four samples per level/binary, not a p99.",
    "Old binary lacks the payload-stat callback; its stat count is unmeasured. Mixed-client testing covers exactly the recorded pair of binaries.",
    "No universal latency, constant-time complexity, payload bandwidth or new 100 GB/TB physical-I/O claim follows from this round."
  ],
